ll as seedling vigor and  weed competitiveness were decided as the  most important traits for growers  we used a fairly straightforward mercury  assisted pedigree selection scheme for  this breeding project with the goal to  introduce disease resistance higher  yield and improved growth habit into the  Calypso and Jacobs cattle heirloom  cultivars using CBB 15 as the other  parents codominant snip markers were  used to select progeny with resistance  to bacterial blight and practice and  being common mosaic virus so the initial  goal was to essentially regain all the  seed traits of the heirloom and release  sort of an improved heirloom cultivar  which is still the plan but many other  interesting phenotypes that you can see  here have also emerged so we will  conduct F for progeny row selection this  field season and that wraps it up it's  been fun  thanks to my lab for all their help my  committee another faculty here at  Cornell whose have contributed input  very grateful to the public being  breeding community which is incredibly  willing to share advice and germplasm  also all the growers  processors and everyone who contributed  ideas as well as my funding sources USDA  nifA  and northeast sare  and you thanks okay  Christians are you doing questions do  you have a question you have a question  that Kristen do you see it yes okay  where all of the varieties you showed  and Ian or were some Mesoamerican so in  terms of our trials which i think is  probably what you're referring to Jeff  so all of these except for Orca which is  right here can you see my screen right  now  I'm not sure no no we see you you're not  sharing anymore right okay so yes there  predominate  mostly there Andean because that is what  is grown in the Northeast they tend to  be determinate and shorter season which  is kind of what's better adapted black  beans for example are Mesoamericans so  so we've been primarily working in  Andean but I think there's a lot of  potential to expand options in the  Mesoamerican gene pool too Thanks does  so does dry bean production in North  East require any specialized equipment  or cancer bean farmers grow dry beans  easily that's a really good question so  the smaller seeded types such as black  beans navy beans generally can be  planted and harvested with the same  combine as soybeans types like kidneys  and cranberries tend to be lower growing  so they're a type 1 determinant instead  of the upright type 2 so those generally  are harvested using a bean puller and  that actually is uprooting the plant and  then it's wind Road into a row and then  combined using a pickup head so it that  does generally require more specialized  equipment ok how many of those I did you  manage at once with marker-assisted  selection and how did you man and  managed population status to deal with  multiple traits so in so this mostly  refers to and up to population which I  grew last summer and so I was a I grew  at about 400 plants and I was selecting  for Tolosa for bacterial blight one  loose eye for BC and the eCos and  essentially what I do  did you know given that I had 400  progeny was to prioritize so BCS and the  is our you know major our gene resistant  so that was kind of the first  requirement  and I essentially selected for either  bacterial blight or you know paired with  be CMV or be CMV and anthracnose to kind  of improve my ability to to advance kind  of those lines thank you  this has been a production of Cornell  University on the web at Cornell edu

